Best Practices Summary
Practice	Implementation
Use defaults/main.yml	Lowest priority variables that users can override
Keep tasks modular	Split into logical files (install.yml, configure.yml)
Include with conditions	Use include_tasks with when for flexibility
Tag everything	Tags for roles, actions, and categories
Validate before applying	Use validate parameter on critical configs
Use handlers properly	Notify only when changes occur
Document dependencies	Clear meta/main.yml with all dependencies
Version your roles	Use Galaxy version or git tags
Test in isolation	Each role should work independently
Secure sensitive data	Use Ansible Vault for passwords, keys
🔧 Troubleshooting
Issue	Solution
Role not found	Check roles_path in ansible.cfg
Variable undefined	Check precedence: is it defined in right file?
Template not found	Path is relative to templates/ in the role
Dependency loop	Check for circular dependencies in meta files
Handler not running	Ensure notify name matches exactly
Tasks skipped	Check tags and when conditions
Permission errors	Verify become: yes in playbook or ansible.cfg
